          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Hipparchus</strong><br>\nHipparchus was born in Nicaea, a city in what is now modern-day Turkey, around 190 BC. He was known for his work in astronomy and mathematics. Even as a young man, he was deeply interested in how the heavens worked and spent much of his life studying the stars and planets.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hipparchus's Interest in Astronomy</strong><br>\nHipparchus's passion for astronomy was driven by his curiosity about celestial phenomena. He observed a lunar eclipse, which led to his interest in understanding the motion of the moon and the sun. His observations were meticulous, and he made detailed notes that would later become invaluable to the field of astronomy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>His Work on the Motion of the Moon</strong><br>\nHipparchus made significant contributions to our understanding of the moon's motion. By carefully recording lunar eclipses, he could make more accurate predictions about their occurrence. His calculations on the irregularity of the moon's orbit were a groundbreaking step in astronomy.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
